+## Current activation (momentum transaction-cost sensitivity on the collected universe — run 46045883943, agent 02, task R-001)
+
+Closed the decision-relevant cost qualification on the only candidate positive
+evidence (short-horizon momentum, ADMITTED AS CANDIDATE POSITIVE EVIDENCE at
+lookback 5 and lookback-robust across 3/5/10). Every prior momentum run used the
+engine's default zero-cost `BacktestConfig`; this activation ran a bounded,
+predeclared transaction-cost sweep and independently verified it.
+
+Method: seed 42; dataset yf-ohlcv-universe-2009-to-2026-10-03; the existing
+`stress_segments` walk-forward regime-stability gate (train=252d/test=84d/
+warmup=60d/overlap=60d, 4 contiguous volatility blocks, min 400 bars/segment)
+with a cost-matched coin-flip null on the same segments; lookbacks {3, 5, 10};
+per-trade notional cost grid {0, 10, 25, 50, 100} bps; decision threshold 25
+bps/trade (~50 bps round trip).
+
+Cost model (the repository's existing `engine.BacktestConfig`): a pre-check
+tooling diagnostic established two engine mechanics that shaped the design —
+(1) the engine's `close +/- slippage` fill is symmetric across buys and sells, so
+the proportional/fixed slippage component cancels over a round trip and does NOT
+accumulate; (2) `commission_per_share` is charged on every fill regardless of
+side, so it is the only accumulating, notional-proportional cost channel. The
+cost grid is therefore expressed as per-trade notional bps and implemented via
+`commission_per_share = (bps/10000) * ref_price`, where `ref_price` is the
+ticker's median close (a cost-calibration constant only — it never enters the
+signal or its timing — fixed before the walk-forward and identical across folds).
+
+A-priori falsification prediction (observed): a mechanical, ~1x-gross,
+daily-rebalanced signal is cost-sensitive, so if the edge were a fair-value/impact
+illusion it should decay toward CONSISTENT_WITH_NOISE as cost rises.
+
+Results:
+- Classification across the 10-asset universe: COST_ROBUST=6 (AAPL, MSFT, GOOGL,
+  AMZN, META, TSLA — positive REGIME_STABLE edge survives the full grid to
+  100 bps/trade), COST_FRAGILE=0, NO_EDGE=4 (NVDA, JPM, JNJ, XOM — exactly the
+  prior lookback NO_EDGE group).
+- Assets whose edge survives to >= 25 bps/trade, by lookback: 7/10 at each of
+  lookback 3, 5, and 10 (consistent — not a single-lookback artifact).
+- The candidate medians degrade only mildly with cost (e.g. TSLA lookback-5
+  [0.132, 0.016, 0.107] at 0 bps -> [0.118, 0.008, 0.108] at 100 bps; META
+  [0.073, 0.067, 0.042] -> [0.062, 0.063, 0.038]); the a-priori cost-decay
+  prediction is REJECTED within the declared conservative grid.
+- Note (verdict-sensitivity, recorded honestly): JPM is REGIME_DEPENDENT at 0 bps
+  (not a clean stable edge) and only becomes REGIME_STABLE at higher cost as the
+  cost compresses cross-segment dispersion; the classifier gates on the 0 bps
+  edge, so JPM is NO_EDGE. The REGIME_STABLE verdict can flip via dispersion
+  compression and must be read alongside the medians.
+
+Independent verification (three gates, all MATCH): Gate 1 fresh `walk_forward` +
+`noise_benchmark` recomputation of AMZN/JPM for all 15 (lookback x cost) median/null
+columns; Gate 2 the cost=0 lookback-5 column reproduces `momentum_results.json`
+exactly (medians, nulls, verdicts) for all 10 tickers; Gate 3 the cost-robustness
+classification and counts re-derive from the artifact and are deterministic.
+Full regression suite: 179 tests, all passing (168 existing + 11 new
+cost-classification unit tests in `tests/test_momentum_cost_sensitivity.py`).
+
+Artifacts: `research/checks/momentum_cost_sensitivity.py` (check),
+`research/checks/verify_momentum_cost_sensitivity.py` (independent verifier),
+`state/check_artifacts/momentum_cost_sensitivity_results.json` (artifact). No
+framework code changed. Research/simulation only; no live trading.
+
+Assessment: the short-horizon momentum edge is cost-robust to 100 bps/trade
+notional cost in the median-fold framework; transaction cost is NOT a
+decision-relevant threat to the candidate within the declared conservative grid.
+The cost-robustness qualification is closed COST_ROBUST. (Caveat for later
+reviews: this is a median-fold, constant-dollar, single-asset-per-book result;
+the mean/tail cost drag on high-turnover folds is larger than the median and is
+not the decision metric here.)
+
+---
+
